<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Omar Ali Saifuddin II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1852</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Omar Ali Saifuddin II was sultan of Brunei from 1828 to 1852. During his reign the English adventurer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-brooke">James Brooke</a> was granted Sarawak and became its rajah in 1841, beginning the loss of Brunei's territories, and in 1846 the island of Labuan was ceded to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> after a British naval attack on the capital. His court was also divided by bitter factional struggles.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/omar-ali-saifuddin-ii.jpg" alt="Omar Ali Saifuddin II" width="320" height="443" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Illustration_of_Sultan_Omar_Ali_Saifuddin_II.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
